# Input for the hash-pinned build tooling lockfile.
#
# PyInstaller is only needed to freeze the app in the build/release jobs. It is
# installed from this hash-locked file (--require-hashes --only-binary :all:)
# instead of `pip install -e .[build]`: the spec files put the project root on
# `pathex`, so the project itself never needs to be pip-installed to build, and
# an editable install would run the local build backend and skip hash pinning.
#
# The lock is universal (Windows + Linux, Python 3.11+) so one file serves the
# Windows and Linux jobs; Windows-only transitives (pefile, pywin32-ctypes) are
# kept behind environment markers. It is constrained to the runtime lock so
# shared transitives (e.g. packaging) never drift from what the app bundles.
#
# Regenerate after editing this file (or when bumping PyInstaller):
#
#   uv pip compile requirements/build-tools.in -c requirements/lock.txt \
#       --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.11 \
#       -o requirements/build-tools.txt

pyinstaller
